     review_date: '2026-10-26'
+scientific_hypotheses:
+  - id: PM1-H1
+    title: Dietary Phosphatidylethanolamine and Neural NAPE/NAE Precursor Supply
+    status: Unestablished
+    proposition: >-
+      Dietary phosphatidylethanolamine may contribute to neural NAPE precursor availability and subsequent
+      N-acylethanolamine formation. Whether this contribution is quantitatively meaningful under ordinary
+      dietary exposure remains unresolved.
+    proposed_direction: Dietary phosphatidylethanolamine → neural NAPE precursor availability → N-acylethanolamine formation
+    rationale: >-
+      Intracellular NAPE precursor biology provides a rationale for examining dietary contribution. Oral
+      delivery to the relevant neural pools and its quantitative importance are not established.
+    finding_links:
+      supporting: []
+      contradictory_or_null: []
+      contextual:
+        - pm_id: BRS-X(ECS-PM1)
+          finding_id: PM1-F1
+          href: '#pm1-f1'
+          explanation: Provides bounded pathway context; does not establish the complete hypothesis.
+    evidence_sources:
+      - study_id: cadas-1997
+        label: Cadas et al. (1997)
+        url: https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6793739/
+        role: contextual
+        proposition: Rat brain and neuronal experiments support intracellular NAPE precursor biology.
+        limitations: Not dietary delivery to neural pools.
+      - study_id: lithander-2008
+        label: Lithander et al. (2008)
+        url: https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2600636/
+        role: contextual
+        proposition: Oral PE-containing exposure did not improve satiety relative to lipid control.
+        limitations: Neural precursor supply was not measured; the behavioural null does not resolve incorporation.
+      - study_id: oatmeal-registration
+        label: Oatmeal trial registration NCT03468179
+        url: https://clinicaltrials.gov/study/NCT03468179
+        role: contextual
+        proposition: The saved citation describes a proposed oatmeal NAPE/NAE experiment.
+        limitations: Not verified results, not oat-bran equivalence or a PE-specific neural delivery result.
+    limitations:
+      - Digestion and remodelling may separate dietary atoms from the intact PE molecule.
+      - >-
+        Trace incorporation alone does not establish meaningful precursor supply, increased pool availability
+        or altered synthesis.
+      - >-
+        PE, NAPE and NAE molecular species must remain distinct; evidence for one does not generalise to all
+        NAEs or anandamide.
+      - Gut or plasma measurements do not establish neural supply.
+      - No increased endocannabinoid signalling, clinical benefit or ordinary-food equivalence is established.
+      - >-
+        The saved oatmeal trial citation describes a proposal, not verified doubled plasma levels; preserve
+        the source-page discrepancy for separate correction.
+      - >-
+        No animal model or arbitrarily selected PE species is part of the core proposition; no experiment is
+        authorised by registration.
+    alternative_explanations:
+      - Endogenous synthesis may dominate neural pools.
+      - Dietary-derived atoms may be recycled without a meaningful contribution to precursor availability.
+    required_evidence:
+      - >-
+        Characterise dietary exposure, digestion, absorption and remodelling and establish contribution to
+        relevant neural NAPE and specified NAE products.
+      - >-
+        Quantify contribution relative to endogenous synthesis and pool turnover; distinguish detectable trace
+        contribution from meaningful supply.
+      - >-
+        Isotope tracing, lipid measurements and controlled exposures are possible methods, not authorised
+        studies.
+      - >-
+        Negligible contribution despite verified exposure counts against meaningful supply under those
+        conditions without rejecting established PE biology.
+    provenance:
+      - >-
+        Author-approved bounded hypothesis following the ten-candidate appraisal and individual review on 14
+        November 2026.
+      - >-
+        Approval registers the proposition only. No dietary admissions, SEC, publication gates, food mappings,
+        rankings or accepted graph edges change.
+    review_date: '2026-11-14'
